# Day 68 – Mobile Devices, Wireless Connectivity, MDM & Help Desk Troubleshooting

## 🎯 Objective

Today's objective was to learn common mobile device technologies, understand wireless connectivity, distinguish device security controls, explore Mobile Device Management (MDM), and practice troubleshooting mobile email and Bluetooth issues.

---

## 1. Mobile Device Fundamentals

Mobile devices include:

- Smartphones
- Tablets
- Company-issued mobile phones
- Other supported portable devices

Common components include:

- Battery and charging port
- Touchscreen and display
- Cameras and microphones
- Wireless network adapters
- Storage
- Operating system

### Common Mobile Operating Systems

- Android
- iOS
- iPadOS

The operating system manages device hardware and provides the platform on which applications run.

---

## 2. Wireless Technologies

### Wi-Fi

Wi-Fi connects a device to a wireless local area network. That network may provide Internet access or access to internal company resources.

### Bluetooth

Bluetooth connects nearby devices, such as wireless headphones, keyboards, mice, and speakers.

### NFC – Near Field Communication

NFC enables communication over a very short distance.

Examples include:

- Contactless payments
- Compatible access cards
- Quick device interactions

### Cellular

Cellular technology connects mobile devices to a mobile carrier's network for services such as mobile data and calls.

### GPS

GPS helps determine a device's location using satellite signals and supporting location technologies.

### Quick Comparison

| Technology | Main purpose |
|---|---|
| Wi-Fi | Connect to a wireless network |
| Bluetooth | Connect nearby accessories |
| NFC | Very short-range communication |
| Cellular | Connect through a mobile carrier |
| GPS | Help determine location |

